From a8aa94645d3467e8d2baecb19ddb913eeafbd931 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chidionyema <377396+chidionyema@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 02:27:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] fix(gateway): write intercepted clarify answers to the
 transcript

While a clarify prompt is pending, the gateway takes any non-slash inbound
text as the answer, hands it to the blocked agent thread in memory and
returns an empty string so adapters do not double-post. Nothing on that path
wrote the text to the message store, and tools/clarify_gateway.py keeps its
entries in RAM only. If the holding turn never flushed a tool result, the
words were gone.

Measured on the founder's own Telegram DM on 2026-08-24: he typed 46
characters at 02:03:02, the gateway logged "intercepted clarify text
response", the turn stalled, and the text was in no store on the machine.
A separate 21-character message went the same way through /steer.

The fix writes a receipt at both interception points. The row is soft
-archived (active=0), so it is on disk and in every transcript export but is
not replayed to the provider - a live user row between an assistant tool
call and its result would break the required message sequence. Recording
never raises, because a failed receipt must not cost the founder the answer
the caller is about to deliver.

append_message gained an active parameter to make that write possible; it
hardcoded 1 before.

Two incident tests, paired per LAW 38: the archived row stays out of the
live conversation and the default write still lands in it; the receipt
reaches disk and a broken write is silent at the caller. All 5 fail on the
pre-fix tree and pass on this one.
